  "package_id": "harmonic-boundary-five",
  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.35.0 proves, for finite simple graphs with certified shortest-path distances and the original strict boundary inequality, that a nonboundary degree-three vertex whose deletion leaves the graph connected forces six boundary vertices; the one-point gluing and block-accounting identities; the 14-vertex sharpness example; all 835 integer infeasibility systems of the local certificate; the bipartite subcubic boundary characterization; a sharp rooted metric truncation theorem; and the grammar weight bounds and polynomial identities for two-trees. A strict audit covers all 15,771 project declarations. The cone coverage, capping reduction, diameter-three argument, subcubic interior reduction, block decomposition, grammar correspondence and catalogue enumerations are conventional proofs and exact computations, replayed by the package checkers and by independent enumerations.",
